/dist/
# The third-party notices GoReleaser's before hooks write into the tree
# (.goreleaser.yaml; docs/release.md): generated from the module cache at
# release time, never committed, and left behind by the local rehearsal
# `goreleaser release --snapshot --clean` -- untracked, which is what
# scripts/release.sh's clean-tree check and GoReleaser's own dirty check
# refuse. Anchored at the root because that is the one place the script writes.
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
/fugaro
# Binaries a `go build` of a main package writes into the root: the CLI, and
# the website's generators under internal/ (go build ./internal/clidoc leaves
# a 74 MB clidoc here). `go run` compiles into the build cache and writes
# nothing, which is what the generators' headers tell a reader to use.
/clidoc
# Windows binaries: a bare `GOOS=windows go build ./cmd/fugaro` writes its
# .exe into the directory it ran in, which is the tree root — and internal/clidoc,
# internal/infra/tf/faketerraform and internal/pricing/catalog/gencatalog for
# the generators. 181 MB of them reached the Windows-port pull request that
# way. Build them with `-o` outside the tree (docs/windows-cli/README.md's
# command writes to $TMPDIR); this rule keeps one from being staged, and
# images/repo_pins_test.go's TestRepositoryTracksNoBuiltBinaries is the pin for
# the case where it was staged anyway.
*.exe
# A local terraform init or test run under deploy/terraform. Set TF_DATA_DIR
# outside the tree instead: go:embed doesn't read .gitignore, and a
# .terraform/ there would put provider binaries in the fugaro binary.
/deploy/terraform/**/.terraform/
/deploy/terraform/**/*.tfstate
/deploy/terraform/**/*.tfstate.*
*.swp
# The website redesign's screenshots: regenerated by
# docs/website/redesign/capture-screenshots.mjs, never committed (see that directory's README).
/docs/website/redesign/current/*.jpg
/docs/website/redesign/after/*.jpg
# Owner-local, never committed: the Firebase CLI's per-project cache and the folder the
# owner keeps signing material and similar secrets in.
/.firebase/
/secrets/
